{
 "schema": "bas-wiresheet/1",
 "id": "hx1-data-freshness",
 "name": "HX-1 Data Freshness",
 "mode": "monitoring",
 "description": "Example: per-point data freshness for a heat exchanger read over Modbus TCP. Monitoring only; invalid or missing readings are data-quality states, never equipment alarms.",
 "equipment": [
  {
   "tag": "HX-1",
   "status": "Commissioning Pending",
   "since": "2026-11-16",
   "source": "site policy"
  }
 ],
 "notes": {
  "integration": "Home Assistant modbus (YAML, packages/hx1_modbus.yaml), hub hx1_t10, scan_interval 15 s.",
  "timestamps": "HA modbus calls async_write_ha_state() on every scan, so State.last_reported advances on every new sample even when the value is unchanged. Verified on production 2026-11-21 13:05 EST via the HA template engine: sensor.hx_1_supply_temp unchanged since 2026-11-20 18:50 EST, last_reported 4.4 s old; the other points 3-14 s. The websocket/REST state views are cached and show last_reported == last_changed for steady values, and state_reported cannot be subscribed over websocket, so the runtime reads last_reported through a 5 s HA template poll. last_changed is never used for freshness.",
  "heartbeat": "sensor.hx_1_oat_watchdog is a T10 countdown refreshed every minute by automation.hx_1_write_oat_to_t10 and read each scan; shown as the T10 link indicator."
 },
